# Rust build output
target/

# ICC profiles are copyrighted works (LEGAL.md §3). Nothing matching *.icc or
# *.icm may enter the repository except fixtures whose provenance is recorded
# in fixtures/reference/PROVENANCE.md, or profiles this project authored.
*.icc
*.icm
!fixtures/**/*.icc
!fixtures/**/*.icm

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# tools/difftest — the lcms2 oracle is pinned, NOT vendored.
#
# Why: lcms2 is a third-party codebase we do not own and do not wish to carry
# in our history. `fetch-lcms2.sh` clones it at the pinned tag into
# tools/difftest/vendor/, which is ignored here. The *pin* (tag + commit hash)
# is committed, in tools/difftest/lcms2.pin; the *source* is not.
#
# Second reason, and the load-bearing one: lcms2's optional plugins
# (plugins/fast_float, plugins/threaded) are GPL-3.0, not MIT. Keeping the
# clone out of the tree keeps GPL-3.0 source out of an MIT repository
# entirely, rather than relying on a build flag to keep it unused.
# See LEGAL.md §4.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
tools/difftest/vendor/

# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
# docs/GHENT_COMPATIBILITY.md — LOCAL ONLY, never committed.
#
# Operator decision, 2026-08-18. The file is the Ghent PDF Output Suite
# workstream in full: which patches are this project's, what the suite's
# readmes say (quoted), where its profiles were extracted to, and what was
# measured against them. That is detailed analysis of, and quotation from, a
# licensed third-party suite whose licence carries an affirmative notice
# requirement and a "commercial context" restriction — see LEGAL.md and the
# file's own §2.2. Keeping it out of an MIT repository avoids creating that
# entanglement at all, rather than relying on a fair-quotation argument.
#
# ★ It is still the reference and it still exists — on this machine, at
# docs/GHENT_COMPATIBILITY.md. Tracked documents cite it by section and
# those citations remain correct for anyone working locally. A reader who
# has only the public repository cannot follow them, and that is the
# accepted cost of the decision, not an oversight.
#
# ★★ This file was tracked and PUBLIC until 533844f. Untracking removes it
# from future commits; it does NOT remove it from history. See
# docs/NEXT_SESSION.md for the outstanding decision on that.
# ------------------------------------------------------------------------
docs/GHENT_COMPATIBILITY.md
